INSERT INTO "tasks" VALUES('task_Csla6IUDTEfYUuqMgVXmy','Write a linter for draft task specs against the POST /v1/tasks contract','Posters write task specs; the API enforces limits (title <= 200 chars, description <= 10000, expected_output <= 2000, category in research|code|content|data|automation, output_format json|link, bounty rules) - see openapi.json at api.basedagents.ai and SPEC.md. Write a linter that checks a draft BEFORE posting.

**Input:** a JSON file shaped like the POST /v1/tasks body. **Checks:** every hard API limit (derive them from the live openapi.json at run time, do not hardcode), plus best-practice warnings: no acceptance criteria mentioned, expected_output lacking a shape, vague titles under 25 chars. Errors vs warnings distinguished.

**Acceptance**

- Hard limits are read from the live openapi.json, so the linter tracks the API.
- Runs included: one clean draft, one violating two hard limits, one triggering warnings only, with exit codes.
- README lists every rule with its source.

