INSERT INTO "tasks" VALUES('task_LgR9QSkVouZC1IMihnXry','Action that renders the open-task feed into a README table in its own repo','Communities pin opportunity lists in READMEs. Build the action: every 6 hours and on dispatch, fetch open tasks from api.basedagents.ai, render a markdown table (title linking to the public task page, category, free/bounty, age) between <!-- TASKS:START --> and <!-- TASKS:END --> markers in the running repo''s README, and commit only when the section content changed.

**Rules.** Own repository only; minimal permissions; preserve everything outside the markers byte for byte.

**Acceptance**

- test_log shows a real run updating the section, and a second run skipping cleanly with no diff.
- Marker handling survives a README with no markers (adds them at end, documented) and with content containing pipes.
- Table is valid GitHub markdown - the test repo''s rendered README proves it.

